<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>LLM Usage</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">LLMs were used solely to aid in polishing the writing and improving the clarity of exposition.
In addition, code-assistant tools were occasionally used for minor programming support, such as code completion and syntax suggestions; they were not employed to design algorithms, generate experiments, or implement the proposed methods from scratch.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Model training configuration</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proxy model, 69M parameters: 4 hidden layers with <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}=256</annotation></semantics></math>, Multi-Head Attention with <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{heads}}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>heads</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{heads}}=4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{kv-heads}}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>kv</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>heads</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{kv-heads}}=4</annotation></semantics></math>, SwiGLU activation function with MLP expansion factor <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathrm{MLP}}=2.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>MLP</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathrm{MLP}}=2.75</annotation></semantics></math>, RoPE with <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=10000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=10000</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, Llama 3 tokenizer with vocabulary size of <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128\,256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128 256</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128\,256</annotation></semantics></math> (after padding) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grattafiori et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, input and output embedding layers are not tied.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 4(12)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>12</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 4(12)</annotation></semantics></math> wider model, 314M (1.3B) parameters: same as proxy, except <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}=1024~(3072)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1024</mn><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3072</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}=1024~(3072)</annotation></semantics></math>. In width scaling, we keep fixed <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{head}}=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>head</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{head}}=64</annotation></semantics></math> and scale the number of heads accordingly.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 8(32)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>32</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 8(32)</annotation></semantics></math> deeper model, 91M (168M) parameters: same as proxy, except 32 (128) hidden layers.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Semi-orthogonal initialization for hidden linear layers and row-wise normalized Gaussian initialization for input/output embedding layers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pethick et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>. Initialisation of the last layer of both MLP and attention blocks (those with the output being added with the residual stream) is multiplied by <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\sqrt{2N_{\mathrm{layers}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>layers</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\sqrt{2N_{\mathrm{layers}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Dropout disabled, no biases in all <span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Linear</span> layers, no weight sharing between input and output embedding layers.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">norm-everywhere</span>: normalise input to every <span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Linear</span> layer via <span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RMSNorm</span> without learnable parameters with <math id="A1.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1e^{-20}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1e^{-20}</annotation></semantics></math>. Effectively, this corresponds to Pre-LN setup with QK-norm plus three additional normalisation layers: V-norm, O-norm (before output projection matrix in Attention block), and MLP-norm (after SwiGLU and before the last MLP layer). Residual connections, including the ones injecting the input embedding layer information, remain intact.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Random seeds:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1.i7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all proxy model runs in Sec. <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Optimal norm transfer ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and Sec. <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Optimal (𝜂,𝐵) scaling rule ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>: <span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">30</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all width/depth-scaled-up model runs: interleaved <span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">30</span> + <span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">3034</span> (every <math id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> step is <span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">30</span>, every other <math id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> step is <span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">3034</span>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For layout scans in Fig. <a href="#S3.F4.sf1" title="Figure 4(a) ‣ Figure 4 ‣ 3.4 Optimal per-layer-group learning rate ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4(a)</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#A1.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ A.12 Learning rate layout for additional batch sizes and horizons ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>: averaging over <span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">30</span> + <span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">3034</span> + <span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">303409</span> for the three “core” learning rate values (<math id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{2^{-4},2^{-6},2^{-8}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2^{-4},2^{-6},2^{-8}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=32</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{2^{-2},2^{-4},2^{-6}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2^{-2},2^{-4},2^{-6}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=128</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{2^{-1},2^{-3},2^{-5}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2^{-1},2^{-3},2^{-5}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=512</annotation></semantics></math>), <span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">3034</span> + <span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">303409</span> for the rest</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For layout scans in Fig. <a href="#S3.F4.sf2" title="Figure 4(b) ‣ Figure 4 ‣ 3.4 Optimal per-layer-group learning rate ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4(b)</span></a>: <span id="A1.I1.i7.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">30</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">torchtitan</span> codebase, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, FSDP2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Feng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, FlashAttention-2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao, 2023</a>)</cite></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Optimizer configuration</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Except dedicated ablations, we use the following set of hyperparameters:</p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unconstrained version (without weight decay),</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Learning rate <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>: grid with <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>0.5</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{0.5}</annotation></semantics></math> step for the proxy model, and <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> step for the width/depth-scaled-up models,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">momentum <math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math>, without Nesterov momentum,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">no warmup, constant learning rate schedule,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1e^{-20}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1e^{-20}</annotation></semantics></math> (used in gradient normalisation),</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">orthogonalization of gradients for hidden layers (<math id="A1.I2.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert.\rVert_{\mathrm{RMS}\to\mathrm{RMS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0.0835em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>RMS</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>RMS</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert.\rVert_{\mathrm{RMS}\to\mathrm{RMS}}</annotation></semantics></math> norm assumption) with Newton-Schulz algorithm for <math id="A1.I2.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{iter}}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>iter</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{iter}}=5</annotation></semantics></math> with original Muon coefficients <math id="A1.I2.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c=(3.4445,-4.7750,2.0315)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3.4445</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4.7750</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2.0315</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c=(3.4445,-4.7750,2.0315)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jordan et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Optimal norm fitting &amp; loss smoothing</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After naïvely taking the empirical optimum across the learning rate grid (e.g. as the one emphasized with dashed black lines in Fig. <a href="#S3.F1.sf1" title="Figure 1(a) ‣ Figure 1 ‣ 3.1 Output norm dynamics ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(a)</span></a>), we found that the corresponding norm scans, although still indicating norm transfer, are quite noisy (e.g. compare Fig. <a href="#S3.F2.sf1" title="Figure 2(a) ‣ Figure 2 ‣ 3.2 Optimal norm transfer ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(a)</span></a> vs. Fig. <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ A.7 Supplementary plots to Fig. ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>a). From Fig. <a href="#S3.F1.sf1" title="Figure 1(a) ‣ Figure 1 ‣ 3.1 Output norm dynamics ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(a)</span></a> we noted that data points in loss vs. norm plot resemble parabola if plotted in log-log scale. Furthermore, we know by design that at initialization (step 0) the output norm equals to 1, and train loss equals to 11.765. With this, we chose to perform a constrained fit with a second-order polynomial function in log-log scale <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(\mathrm{loss})=a\log(\mathrm{norm})^{2}+b\log(\mathrm{norm})+c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>loss</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>norm</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>norm</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(\mathrm{loss})=a\log(\mathrm{norm})^{2}+b\log(\mathrm{norm})+c</annotation></semantics></math>, where the free term <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed at precisely the loss value at initialization. We do this using weighted least squares fitting with <span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">np.linalg.lstsq</span>, where the weighting is done with inverse uncertainties coming from <span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">loss smoothing</span>, described below. For robustness, only seven data points around the empirical optimum are used in the fit. The optimal loss and norm values are then extracted as the parabola optimum coordinates. Optimal learning rate is taken from the data point closest to the fitted optimum. Results of such fits for Fig. <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.2 Optimal norm transfer ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> can be found in Fig. <a href="#A1.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ A.13 Individual norm scans and fits ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since running several random seeds is computationally intensive, we perform <span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">loss smoothing</span> to estimate the loss variance and make loss estimates more robust. Essentially, for a given horizon point, instead of taking its loss value, we average it with the previous and next evaluated points (67M tokens away, or e.g. 128 steps from each other with <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=128</annotation></semantics></math>). Empirically estimated standard deviation is then used in the fits as described above. We employ loss smoothing only for small batch sizes <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\leq 128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\leq 128</annotation></semantics></math>, as those having large loss variance, and for large token horizons <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\geq 2^{33}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>33</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\geq 2^{33}</annotation></semantics></math>, to stay in the region of largely converged loss (which can be locally linearly approximated) and therefore not bias the estimate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In order to get variance estimate in Fig. <a href="#S3.F3.sf2" title="Figure 3(b) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 3.3 Optimal (𝜂,𝐵) scaling rule ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a> without running several random seed runs, we vary the fitting procedure outlined above (with/without fitting, with/without loss smoothing, with/without constraint to loss at initialization), thus resulting in 6 total variations. For each of those we track how optimal norm/loss/learning rate changes, and propagate this variance to plotting and downstream analysis.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Distributed Scion</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implemented a distributed version of Scion/Muon. In this section, we briefly describe the implementation. We assume that the vectorized momentum buffer update is performed before applying the actual weight update.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.1 </span>DDP-Disco</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a warm-up, we first consider the DDP case (note that a DDP-based version of Muon has already been implemented in <span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">modded-nanogpt<span id="footnote10" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">10</span></span>
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                <a href="https://github.com/KellerJordan/modded-nanogpt" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url">https://github.com/KellerJordan/modded-nanogpt</a></span></span></span></span>). Our implementation differs slightly from theirs, as we do not explicitly apply communication–computation overlap for DDP.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Disco <span id="algorithm1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">step_ddp</span></figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.6.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Parameters <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=|\{p\}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=|\{p\}|</annotation></semantics></math>, world size <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, local rank <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.2" class="ltx_listingline">bucket_size <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow M</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.3" class="ltx_listingline">total_buckets <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\lceil P/M\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\lceil P/M\rceil</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">global_updates</span> <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> array of length <math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm1.6.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Step 1: Compute local updates  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm1.6.6.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm1.6.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.6.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.6.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm1.6.7.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\bmod M=r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\bmod M=r</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.6.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{GetMomentum}(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">GetMomentum</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{GetMomentum}(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{LMO}(g_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">LMO</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{LMO}(g_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.6.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">global_updates</span>[<math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>] <math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm1.6.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Step 2: Communicate updates in buckets  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.12" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm1.6.12.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm1.6.12.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> total_buckets <math id="algorithm1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.6.12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.6.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">start_idx</span> <math id="algorithm1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow b\cdot M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow b\cdot M</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.6.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">end_idx</span> <math id="algorithm1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\min(\textit{start\_idx}+M,\ P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">start_idx</mtext><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\min(\textit{start\_idx}+M,\ P)</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.6.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">my_idx</span> <math id="algorithm1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm1.6.15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">start_idx</span> <math id="algorithm1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+r</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.16" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.6.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm1.6.16.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">my_idx <math id="algorithm1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> end_idx</em> <span id="algorithm1.6.16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.17" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\text{send}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mtext>send</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\text{send}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm1.6.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">global_updates</span>[<span id="algorithm1.6.17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">my_idx</span>] ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.18" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.6.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.19" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{\text{send}}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mtext>send</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{\text{send}}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.20" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u_{j}\}_{j=0}^{M-1}\leftarrow\textsc{AllGather}(u_{\text{send}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">AllGather</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mtext>send</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u_{j}\}_{j=0}^{M-1}\leftarrow\textsc{AllGather}(u_{\text{send}})</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.21" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.6.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm1.6.21.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm1.6.21.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> end_idx <math id="algorithm1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math> start_idx <math id="algorithm1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.6.21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.22" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.6.22.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">global_updates</span>[<span id="algorithm1.6.22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">start_idx</span> <math id="algorithm1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+j</annotation></semantics></math>] <math id="algorithm1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow u_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow u_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.23" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.23.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm1.6.23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Step 3: Apply updates vectorized  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.24" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.24.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ApplyUpdates</span>(<math id="algorithm1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1},</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm1.6.24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">global_updates</span>) ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.25" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Helper functions:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GetMomentum</span>(<math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>): returns the momentum of <math id="A1.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> from the momentum buffer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LMO</span>(<math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>): runs the LMO based on the chosen norm of <math id="A1.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AllGather</span>(<math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>): gathers one tensor <math id="A1.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> from each rank in the data-parallel group.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ApplyUpdates</span>(<math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p\},\{u\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p\},\{u\}</annotation></semantics></math>): applies the global updates <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{u\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{u\}</annotation></semantics></math> to the parameters <math id="A1.I3.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p\}</annotation></semantics></math> in a single vectorized operation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Notice this version works out-of-the-box for PP+DDP, as we could let each PP(Pipeline Parallelism) stage only manage the parts of the model that the current PP stages needed for forward and backward.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To make it work with TP, one needs to do an extra all-gather in the local update loop.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.2 </span>FSDP-Disco</h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, “FSDP” refers to a combination of <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FSDP2</span> with arbitrary parallelisms, including Data Parallelism (DP), Context Parallelism (CP), Expert Parallelism (EP), Tensor Parallelism (TP), and Pipeline Parallelism (PP). In this section, we restrict our discussion to FSDP and EP (via DP2EP). In principle, there is no need to treat DP and PP separately: one only needs to all-gather the full gradient before communication in the FSDP case to ensure compatibility with TP.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We assume the design of this work, which applies an <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert.\rVert_{1\to\mathrm{RMS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0.0835em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>RMS</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert.\rVert_{1\to\mathrm{RMS}}</annotation></semantics></math> norm for the LLM’s embedding layer and an <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert.\rVert_{\mathrm{RMS}\to\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0.0835em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>RMS</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert.\rVert_{\mathrm{RMS}\to\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> norm for the output linear layer. (<span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SignNorm</span> is also acceptable and remains compatible if one strictly follows Scion’s design.)</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FSDP2</span> implementation in PyTorch shards weights and gradients along the tensor’s first dimension. We discuss Disco under this assumption and further assume that each tensor or matrix corresponds to a single layer. Consequently, fused tensors such as <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fused_QKV</span> in attention layers or <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fused_W13</span> in SwiGLU are not supported.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Under these hypotheses, we can classify parameters into three groups: <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">embedding</span>, <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">experts</span>, and (pure-)<span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fsdp</span>. For updates, no extra communication is required for <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">embedding</span> and <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">experts</span> parameters, thanks to the <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Shard(0)</span> strategy in <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">FSDP2</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>Disco <span id="algorithm2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">step_embedding</span></figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.6.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Embedding parameters <math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm2.6.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Initialise updates storage  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">updates</span> <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> array of length <math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm2.6.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">get momentum and compute LMO update on local shards  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm2.6.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm2.6.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.6.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{GetMomentum}(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">GetMomentum</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{GetMomentum}(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{LMO}(g_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">LMO</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{LMO}(g_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm2.6.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">updates</span>[<math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>] <math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm2.6.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Apply updates vectorized  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.10" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.6.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ApplyUpdates</span>(<math id="algorithm2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1},\ \textit{updates}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">updates</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1},\ \textit{updates}</annotation></semantics></math>) ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.6.11" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="algorithm3" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span>Disco <span id="algorithm3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">step_experts</span></figcaption>
<div id="algorithm3.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm3.6.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm3.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm3.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Expert parameters <math id="algorithm3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, transpose flag <span id="algorithm3.6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">transpose</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm3.6.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Initialise updates storage  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">updates</span> <math id="algorithm3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> array of length <math id="algorithm3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm3.6.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">get momentum and compute LMO update on local shards  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm3.6.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm3.6.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm3.6.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{GetMomentum}(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">GetMomentum</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{GetMomentum}(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{BatchedLMO}(g_{i};\ \textit{transpose\_experts}=\textit{transpose})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">BatchedLMO</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">transpose_experts</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">transpose</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{BatchedLMO}(g_{i};\ \textit{transpose\_experts}=\textit{transpose})</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm3.6.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">updates</span>[<math id="algorithm3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>] <math id="algorithm3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm3.6.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Apply updates vectorized  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.10" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm3.6.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ApplyUpdates</span>(<math id="algorithm3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1},\ \textit{updates}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">updates</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1},\ \textit{updates}</annotation></semantics></math>) ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm3.6.11" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Noting that MoE expert weights are typically laid out as either
<math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{total\_experts},d_{\text{out}},d_{\text{in}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total_experts</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{total\_experts},d_{\text{out}},d_{\text{in}})</annotation></semantics></math> or
<math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{total\_experts},d_{\text{in}},d_{\text{out}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>total_experts</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{total\_experts},d_{\text{in}},d_{\text{out}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply a transpose in the latter case to ensure that the output dimension comes first.
In an FSDP + DP2EP setting, each gradient passed to <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LMO</span> is therefore a 3D tensor with layout
<math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{local\_experts},d_{\text{out}},d_{\text{in}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>local_experts</mtext><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>in</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{local\_experts},d_{\text{out}},d_{\text{in}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Accordingly, SVD or Newton-Schulz-based algorithms must correctly handle batched inputs.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">And below is the algorithm for purely fsdp-shard parameters.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm4" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 4</span> </span>Disco <span id="algorithm4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">step_fsdp</span></figcaption>
<div id="algorithm4.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm4.6.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm4.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm4.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>FSDP-sharded parameters <math id="algorithm4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, world size <math id="algorithm4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> over <span id="algorithm4.6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fsdp</span>, local rank <math id="algorithm4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.2" class="ltx_listingline">bucket_size <math id="algorithm4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow M</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.3" class="ltx_listingline">total_buckets <math id="algorithm4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\lceil P/M\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\lceil P/M\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">global_updates</span> <math id="algorithm4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> array of length <math id="algorithm4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm4.6.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm4.6.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> total_buckets <math id="algorithm4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.6.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.6.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">start</span> <math id="algorithm4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow b\cdot M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow b\cdot M</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="algorithm4.6.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">end</span> <math id="algorithm4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\min(\textit{start}+M,\ P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">start</mtext><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\min(\textit{start}+M,\ P)</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.6.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">my_idx</span> <math id="algorithm4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\textit{start}+r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">start</mtext><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\textit{start}+r</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.6.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm4.6.8.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm4.6.8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.6.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow\textit{start}+j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">start</mtext><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow\textit{start}+j</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.6.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm4.6.10.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;\textit{end}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">end</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;\textit{end}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.6.10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{GetMomentum}(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">GetMomentum</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}\leftarrow\textsc{GetMomentum}(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="algorithm4.6.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm4.6.11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">row-sharded by FSDP</span>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.6.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">send_list</span>[j] <math id="algorithm4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.6.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.6.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">send_list</span>[j] <math id="algorithm4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="algorithm4.6.14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm4.6.14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">zero padding</span>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{recv\_list}\leftarrow\textsc{AllToAll}(\textit{send\_list})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">recv_list</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">AllToAll</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">send_list</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{recv\_list}\leftarrow\textsc{AllToAll}(\textit{send\_list})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.16" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\star}\leftarrow\textsc{ConcatRows}(\textit{recv\_list})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">ConcatRows</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">recv_list</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\star}\leftarrow\textsc{ConcatRows}(\textit{recv\_list})</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="algorithm4.6.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm4.6.16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reconstruct full gradient for <math id="algorithm4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i^{\star}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i^{\star}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.17" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="algorithm4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\star}\leftarrow\textsc{LMO}(g^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">LMO</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\star}\leftarrow\textsc{LMO}(g^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.18" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.6.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">updates_send_list</span> <math id="algorithm4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\textsc{SplitRows}(u^{\star},\ M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SplitRows</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\textsc{SplitRows}(u^{\star},\ M)</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="algorithm4.6.18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm4.6.18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">split <math id="algorithm4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> by rows</span>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.19" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.6.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">updates_recv_list</span> <math id="algorithm4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\textsc{AllToAll}(\textit{updates\_send\_list})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">AllToAll</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">updates_send_list</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\textsc{AllToAll}(\textit{updates\_send\_list})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.20" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.6.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm4.6.20.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm4.6.20.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> end <math id="algorithm4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math> start <math id="algorithm4.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm4.6.20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.21" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm4.6.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">global_updates</span>[<span id="algorithm4.6.21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">start</span> + j] <math id="algorithm4.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm4.6.21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">updates_recv_list</span>[j];
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.22" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.22.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/* </span><span id="algorithm4.6.22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Single vectorized apply  */</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.23" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm4.6.23.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ApplyUpdates</span>(<math id="algorithm4.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{i}\}_{i=0}^{P-1},</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm4.6.23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">global_updates</span>);
</div>
<div id="algorithm4.6.24" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Helper functions:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AllToAll</span>(<span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">list</span>): list-based <span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AllToAll</span> over <span id="A1.I4.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">dp_shard_cp</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ConcatRows</span>(<span id="A1.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">list</span>): concatenates row-shards into a full tensor.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SplitRows</span>(<math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,M</annotation></semantics></math>): splits <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A1.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> contiguous row blocks.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
