B</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is 128 for both <math id="A1.F11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=2^{31}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>31</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=2^{31}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.F11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=2^{33}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>33</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=2^{33}</annotation></semantics></math> according to Fig. <a href="#S3.F3.sf2" title="Figure 3(b) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 3.3 Optimal (𝜂,𝐵) scaling rule ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a>. </figcaption>
</figure>
