<figure id="A1.F12.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03871v1/fits-x32-d-from-fit-True.svg" id="A1.F12.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/84;" width="548" height="84"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span><span id="A1.F12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Individual norm scans for various batch sizes <math id="A1.F12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (columns), across various horizons <math id="A1.F12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> in (a), across various models in (b) (rows).</span> We plot train loss (Y-axis) against the output layer operator norm <math id="A1.F12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert{\bm{W}}_{\mathrm{out}}\rVert_{\mathrm{RMS}\to\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>RMS</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert{\bm{W}}_{\mathrm{out}}\rVert_{\mathrm{RMS}\to\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each point corresponds to a different learning rate run and error bars correspond to loss smoothing variance (see Appendix <a href="#A1.SS4" title="A.4 Optimal norm fitting &amp; loss smoothing ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>). The best-loss point for each <math id="A1.F12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B,D)</annotation></semantics></math> is pinpointed with the blue dashed line, fitted curves are shown with blue solid lines. These fit results are used for: <span id="A1.F12.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(a)</span> Fig. <a href="#S3.F2.sf1" title="Figure 2(a) ‣ Figure 2 ‣ 3.2 Optimal norm transfer ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(a)</span></a> and Fig. <a href="#S3.F3.sf2" title="Figure 3(b) ‣ Figure 3 ‣ 3.3 Optimal (𝜂,𝐵) scaling rule ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3(b)</span></a>,
<span id="A1.F12.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(b)</span> Fig. <a href="#S3.F2.sf2" title="Figure 2(b) ‣ Figure 2 ‣ 3.2 Optimal norm transfer ‣ 3 Results ‣ Optimal Scaling Needs Optimal Norm" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2(b)</span></a>, from top to bottom rows: proxy, <math id="A1.F12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 4</annotation></semantics></math>-width, <math id="A1.F12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 12</annotation></semantics></math>-width, <math id="A1.F12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 8</annotation></semantics></math>-depth, <math id="A1.F12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 32</annotation></semantics></math>-depth.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F13" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F13.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03871v1/fits-base-from-fit-False-momentum-0.1-decayed-False.svg" id="A1.F13.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/335;" width="548" height="335"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F13.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.03871v1/fits-base-from-fit-False-momentum-0.1-decayed-True.svg" id="A1.F13.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/335;" width="548" height="335"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span><span id="A1.F13.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Individual output norm <math id="A1.F13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert{\bm{W}}_{\mathrm{out}}\rVert_{\mathrm{RMS}\to\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>RMS</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert{\bm{W}}_{\mathrm{out}}\rVert_{\mathrm{RMS}\to\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> scans for various batch sizes <math id="A1.F13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (columns) across various horizons <math id="A1.F13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> (rows).</span>
<span id="A1.F13.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(a)</span> with momentum = 0.1, no learning rate decay.
<span id="A1.F13.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(b)</span> with momentum = 0.1, with learning rate decay linearly to 0 for 25% of total horizon.</figcaption>
</figure>
